/**
 * Clears CE0066 "Entity access is out of date" on OpenAIConnector's domain model.
 *
 * `mxcli marketplace install 220472` (OpenAI Connector 9.1.0 — 9.0.0 too) leaves
 * the module's domain model with that error, and it blocks the build, not just
 * `mx check`. Studio Pro's "Update security" button is the interactive fix.
 *
 * Two things that did NOT work, in case someone tries them again:
 *
 *   1. Re-issuing the grants in place. mxcli's GRANT adds and modifies member
 *      entries but never removes one, so a stale entry survives the rewrite.
 *   2. REVOKE followed by a fresh GRANT. The rules mxcli then builds trigger
 *      CE0066 by themselves — verified by revoking the six Administrator rules
 *      (error persisted against mxcli-authored User rules) and then the four
 *      User rules (error cleared). Every one of these entities specializes a
 *      GenAICommons entity, and mxcli's rule builder lists inherited members;
 *      Mendix appears not to accept that here.
 *
 * So this removes OpenAIConnector's ten entity access rules and does not put
 * them back. The two module roles themselves survive, along with their page and
 * microflow access.
 *
 * WHAT THIS COSTS: nothing while project security is OFF, which is this app's
 * setting — entity access rules are not enforced at that level. The moment
 * security is raised to Prototype or Production, OpenAIConnector's entity access
 * has to be restored in Studio Pro ("Update security" in its domain model), or
 * its admin pages will show empty data.
 *
 * Not idempotent: a second run errors on rules that are already gone.
 */

revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."ApiKey";
revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."AzureAISearchResource";
revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."Configuration";
revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."ConfigurationTest";
revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."Index";
revoke OpenAIConnector.Administrator on OpenAIConnector."OpenAIDeployedModel";

revoke OpenAIConnector.User on OpenAIConnector."AzureAISearchResource";
revoke OpenAIConnector.User on OpenAIConnector."Configuration";
revoke OpenAIConnector.User on OpenAIConnector."Index";
revoke OpenAIConnector.User on OpenAIConnector."OpenAIDeployedModel";
